      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, that's a really good breakdown of how they structure those arguments. it's helpful to see how they try to bridge the gap between physical evolution and cognitive performance. \n\njust to make sure i have the full picture for my rebuttal: when people use these arguments to claim there is a \"biological hierarchy,\" do they usually frame it in terms of a \"civilizational\" impact? like, how do they use these supposed biological differences to explain why certain races have historically dominated or led in terms of technology, government, or global influence? i want to understand how they connect individual genetics to the broader history of human civilization.",
